How To Add a Subfolder named like "image" 

Steps:
- At GitHub, navigate to your destination repo
- Click the (+) Add file button, 
- Select "Create new file".

In the filename field, type 
```
image/.gitkeep (or any filename after **image/**). 
This will create the image subfolder.
```
Add some contents (it can be empty), then commit the new file.

Note: 
Git only tracks folders if they contain files, 
Thus, adding an empty file like
```
/main-folder/.gitkeep 
```
is a common practice to keep empty folders in your repository.

-->
